WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.836
- About 280 Canadians had
their accounts frozen,

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:07.506 align:start size:88% position:13%
and so what that
looked like was mothers

00:00:07.506 --> 00:00:09.542 align:start size:84% position:16%
stuck at the grocery
store checkout

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.944 align:start size:84% position:16%
that had to leave
their groceries there,

00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:14.748
which is a mortifying
experience in itself.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.249
Like you just said, you know,

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:17.951 align:start size:97% position:3%
parents that couldn't buy
medicine for their children,

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:19.152
couldn't pay their mortgage,

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.920 align:start size:81% position:19%
couldn't pay their
child support.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.924
I mean, I was arrested and
my husband was in Ottawa.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.626
We had a joint account.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:28.828
I mean, we don't anymore,
but we had a joint account.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.030
So here he is in a strange
city, doesn't know anyone,

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.866
and has no access to funds.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.435
(light music)

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.708 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I'm Dave Rubin,
and joining me today

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.877
is one of the key organizers

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:46.012
of the Canadian trucker protests

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.348
and author of "Hold the Line:

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:51.951
My Story from the Heart
of the Freedom Convoy."

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.953
Tamara Lich, welcome
to "The Rubin Report."

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.255 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Thank you so
much for having me.

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:56.790
- I am glad to have you.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.859 align:start size:97% position:3%
You came down to the free
state of Florida to do this.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.728
We could have done it on Skype,

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.629 align:start size:84% position:16%
but you wanted to
feel a little freedom.

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:05.431 align:start size:84% position:16%
You wanted to
breathe that freedom,

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:07.433
that beautiful thing that
we have here, didn't you?

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:08.667
- Absolutely. (laughs)

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:09.902
- Yeah, that's a
little different

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:11.070
than what you have
going on Canada.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.438 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It's very different,
very different.

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:13.706
Yes. Yeah.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.875
- So, well, let's just
start at the beginning

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.678 align:start size:84% position:16%
because I suspect that
you did not intend

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.513
maybe five years
ago to be a leader

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.548
of a Canadian trucker convoy.

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.784
I don't think you intended to
have to write a book about it.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.885
I don't think you intended
to have to have your lawyer

00:01:26.885 --> 00:01:30.022 align:start position:0%
in the studio with us right
now and a bunch of other stuff.

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:33.193 align:start size:88% position:13%
So just tell me a little
bit about yourself

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.627
and then kind of what led you

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:37.196 align:start size:84% position:16%
to the Covid moment
where then you stepped

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:38.831 align:start size:81% position:19%
into a whole bunch
of other stuff.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.400 align:start size:84% position:16%
Then we'll spend
most of the interview

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.234
talking about that, obviously.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.802
- Yeah, sounds great.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:45.605
Well, I was born and raised
on the prairies in Canada,

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:46.873
the prairie provinces,

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:49.342 align:start size:84% position:16%
and predominantly
work in oil and gas,

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:52.378
so very heavy in the
energy sector there.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:55.882
And it was through that that
I started to kind of wake up

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:57.951 align:start size:97% position:3%
to what was going on, because
the Canadian government

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:00.053
is really pushing this net zero

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.321 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they were
crushing our economy,

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:04.390
and they were putting
through legislation

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.858
that was harming families.

00:02:05.858 --> 00:02:07.126
People were losing jobs,

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:10.763
and so I became, I
guess an activist.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.565 align:start size:97% position:3%
We started going to rallies
and stuff like that,

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:15.367
and of course I also was
following very closely

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:19.072 align:start position:0%
what was happening at a federal
level with our politicians.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:21.941
And then of course, covid hit,

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:25.611
and I'm not sure about what it
was like down in the States,

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:29.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
but in Canada it was
very dark and depressing.

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:30.750
We were segregated, you know.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.152
I was told my parents weren't
even allowed in my own home

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:36.222
or my children, which
did not work for me.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:40.159
And people I knew and cared
about were getting affected.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:43.863 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, the suicides in
my hometown were so numerous

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.165
they stopped reporting on them.

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:47.767
And that's the kind of
stories that we heard,

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.235 align:start size:81% position:19%
you know, going
all across Canada.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:52.772 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I wanted to do
something and get involved,

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:56.042
and I made a phone
call to Chris Barber,

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:58.378
and now here I am. (laughs)

00:02:58.378 --> 00:03:00.679
- So a lot has transpired
over the last couple years.

00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:02.047
- Yes.

00:03:02.047 --> 00:03:03.515 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You know, it was
interesting for me because,

00:03:03.515 --> 00:03:05.485
you know, every day I wake
up and there's another story,

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:08.721
and especially during Covid,
another crazy thing happening.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.424
But I was noticing that more
and more people from Canada

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:12.892
were tuning into the show
when I was just talking

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:15.027 align:start size:88% position:13%
about the covid
craziness in the States.

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:17.797 align:start position:0%
And then suddenly this
Canadian trucker thing happens,

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:20.633
and then it becomes kind
of a worldwide phenomenon.

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.101
So first, can you just
talk a little bit more

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:25.437
about how draconian
all of the lockdowns

00:03:25.437 --> 00:03:27.439
and everything were in
Canada, and you guys,

00:03:27.439 --> 00:03:29.675 align:start size:88% position:13%
you don't have a federal
system like we do,

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:31.711
so it was pretty
much countrywide.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.212
- It was very much countrywide.

00:03:33.212 --> 00:03:36.014
We were dealing with some...

00:03:36.014 --> 00:03:39.985 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, our prime minister made
the vaccine a wedge issue

00:03:39.985 --> 00:03:41.487
in the last election,

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:45.324
and so he was like, he came
off like a lunatic, you know?

00:03:45.324 --> 00:03:46.259
He was out there.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.526
"If you're not vaccinated,

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:50.062
you can't get on a
train or a plane."

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:52.898 align:start size:84% position:16%
People were being
denied medical care.

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:54.601 align:start size:84% position:16%
In Quebec, the
province of Quebec,

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:57.503
they were going to
initiate a vax tax.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.472
You know, they had
curfews in Quebec.

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:02.475
And that was across
the whole country

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:04.176
this stuff was happening.

00:04:04.176 --> 00:04:06.412
And like I said, you
know, something so
simple as, you know,

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.414
not being allowed to
have your own family

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.683
in your own home, you know?

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:11.918
People lost their jobs.

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:13.986
They lost their businesses.

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:17.723 align:start size:84% position:16%
Loved ones were dying
by themselves in
long-term care homes.

00:04:17.723 --> 00:04:19.925
They weren't even allowed
to go in to say goodbye

00:04:19.925 --> 00:04:21.760
to their dying parents.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:25.364
So it was unacceptable.

00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:26.599
Unacceptable.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.101 align:start size:81% position:19%
And something that
I never thought

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:29.602
I would see happen in Canada.

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.804
You know, never before in our
history have we quarantined

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:34.173 align:start size:84% position:16%
the healthy to save
the vulnerable.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.508
So.

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.610 align:start size:84% position:16%
- What do you think
was the breaking point

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
that got the trucker
thing to get going there?

00:04:40.946 --> 00:04:42.748
Because when people
think about Canada,

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:46.819
they think about John Candy
and they think about comedy

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.821
and they, you know, like Canada,

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:51.991
they think about poutine and
Mounties and pleasant people

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:53.525
that just aren't, you know.

00:04:53.525 --> 00:04:55.027
I love going to Canada.

00:04:55.027 --> 00:04:57.997
Like everyone's very pleasant
and nice and all that stuff.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:59.899 align:start size:97% position:3%
You don't think of the
Canadians as being the people

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:01.133
that are gonna push back.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:02.368
- Mm-hm. Exactly.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:03.302
- And maybe that's
what the government

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:04.804
was preying on, actually.

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:07.473
- Yeah, I don't think that
they saw that coming at all.

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:09.675
So when the government of Canada

00:05:09.675 --> 00:05:11.511
was going to initiate
the trucker mandate,

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:14.714
which was gonna prevent
cross-border travel,

00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:15.547
well, it wouldn't prevent it.

00:05:15.547 --> 00:05:16.749
What it was gonna do

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.250 align:start size:88% position:13%
was if you did not have
a vaccine passport,

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:21.287 align:start size:97% position:3%
then you would have to go home
and quarantine for 14 days.

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:23.188
And so along our border,

00:05:23.188 --> 00:05:26.392 align:start size:97% position:3%
we have a lot of truckers
that are back and forth daily.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.227 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, they can't
take that kind of a hit.

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:30.730
They couldn't afford
that kind of a hit.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:33.099
And so they have
families to feed.

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:34.567 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so that was
really the catalyst

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.502
that started the whole thing.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:40.806 align:start position:0%
And my good friend Chris Barber
did a TikTok video calling

00:05:40.806 --> 00:05:43.542
for a shutdown on
January the 23rd

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:46.879 align:start size:97% position:3%
and a lady trucker named
Brigitte Belton from Ontario

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:50.515
had reached out to him,
and then just this group,

00:05:50.515 --> 00:05:53.453 align:start size:97% position:3%
a small group of people
came together and, you know,

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:55.187
we all had very similar ideas,

00:05:55.187 --> 00:05:58.724 align:start size:97% position:3%
and in 10 days we
organized this entire thing

00:05:58.724 --> 00:05:59.959
and drove cross country.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:01.393
- So you're driving
cross-country and now

00:06:01.393 --> 00:06:03.496 align:start size:97% position:3%
the mainstream media is
calling you a bunch of racists

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:04.931
and bigots and Justin Trudeau

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:06.299
said that you were transphobes.

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:07.867
I mean, it was really like-

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:08.801
- Everything.

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:11.003
- It was everything at once.

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:12.238
What was the hope?

00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:13.906
Like when you all
began the thing,

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:16.042 align:start size:84% position:16%
was the hope really
to break the...

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:17.042
Was it to break the government?

00:06:17.042 --> 00:06:18.477
Was it to break Trudeau?

00:06:18.477 --> 00:06:19.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it just to turn
around all the lockdowns?

00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:21.447
Like...

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:23.649
- The only reason we went
was to end the mandates.

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:24.584
That's it.

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.119 align:start size:84% position:16%
Yeah, there was
lots of crazy rumors

00:06:27.119 --> 00:06:29.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we were going to
overthrow the government.

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:30.589
And I mean, it was awful.

00:06:30.589 --> 00:06:32.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
- You guys were picking
up trash after yourselves.

00:06:32.224 --> 00:06:34.259 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like it was so
ridiculously peaceful.

00:06:34.259 --> 00:06:35.661
- It was amazing.

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:37.597 align:start position:0%
It was one of the most beautiful
experiences of my life,

00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:40.066
a beautiful show of humanity.

00:06:40.066 --> 00:06:43.536 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, everybody
that came to the convoy

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:45.037
was basically a volunteer

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:47.940
because nobody came there
without donating something,

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.542 align:start size:97% position:3%
bringing something,
contributing or pitching in,

00:06:50.542 --> 00:06:53.545
and like you said, shoveling
snow or cleaning up garbage,

00:06:53.545 --> 00:06:56.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
or, you know, it was,
everyone was a volunteer.

00:06:56.115 --> 00:06:57.850
Everyone was an organizer.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.486
- So the thing that I think
really put it on the map,

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:02.287
first, they're calling
you racists and bigots

00:07:02.287 --> 00:07:03.522
and the rest of it.

00:07:03.522 --> 00:07:05.358
But okay, we've all
been through that,

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:08.861 align:start size:84% position:16%
but then this bank
account thing happens.

00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:10.328
So talk about that.

00:07:10.328 --> 00:07:12.965 align:start position:0%
Did you have any sense that
something like this was coming?

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:14.366
How did that get laid out?

00:07:14.366 --> 00:07:15.568
How did it affect you?

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:18.804 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, as we were
dealing with GoFundMe,

00:07:18.804 --> 00:07:22.407 align:start size:97% position:3%
that was the initial crowdfund
platform that we used,

00:07:22.407 --> 00:07:25.711
and we had an accountant come
in and he was actually trying

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:28.748 align:start size:97% position:3%
to set up a bank account
for us to prevent that money

00:07:28.748 --> 00:07:30.583 align:start size:88% position:13%
from going into,
'cause I just set it up

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:33.752
to go into one of my
personal bank accounts.

00:07:33.752 --> 00:07:37.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so TD Bank was really
dragging their feet,

00:07:37.422 --> 00:07:39.191
dragging their feet,
dragging their feet.

00:07:39.191 --> 00:07:41.660
So, I sensed that
something was up.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:43.829
And then of course, as soon
as GoFundMe released it,

00:07:43.829 --> 00:07:46.532 align:start size:84% position:16%
they pretty much
grabbed it right away,

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:48.067
seized it immediately.

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:51.904
- So basically GoFundMe
was taking the money.

00:07:51.904 --> 00:07:54.873 align:start size:84% position:16%
You were first putting
it to your account,

00:07:54.873 --> 00:07:56.375
but then you were
like, "All right,

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:59.211
I wanna put this to the actual
separate account for the..."

00:07:59.211 --> 00:08:01.447 align:start size:81% position:19%
Is it a nonprofit,
or what was it?

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:03.916
- Well, we did set up
an nonprofit after,

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:06.485
but at that time we didn't
have a board of directors.

00:08:06.485 --> 00:08:09.020
We did that actually
in Ottawa on the fly,

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:11.023
create the board of directors
so that we could make sure

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:12.825
that it was all managed and...

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:16.495
- And then TD shut
you down before,

00:08:16.495 --> 00:08:18.197
'cause GoFundMe shut
you down too, right?

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:19.664
- Yes, they did.

00:08:19.664 --> 00:08:21.700 align:start size:97% position:3%
We had a fantastic meeting,
actually, with GoFundMe

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:23.368
on a Thursday night.

00:08:23.368 --> 00:08:24.470
Our lawyers were there.

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:26.272
Their lawyers were there.

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:29.608
And we left that meeting, I
left that meeting anyways,

00:08:29.608 --> 00:08:30.843
feeling very hopeful,

00:08:30.843 --> 00:08:32.344
like we'd answered
all their questions,

00:08:32.344 --> 00:08:35.447
and the next afternoon
they froze the campaign.

00:08:35.447 --> 00:08:37.450
So yeah.

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:41.387
And then, credit to the
governor of Florida.

00:08:41.387 --> 00:08:43.722 align:start size:88% position:13%
I hope I get to shake
that man's hand one day.

00:08:43.722 --> 00:08:44.923
GoFundMe was going to...

00:08:44.923 --> 00:08:46.391
They came out and said,

00:08:46.391 --> 00:08:49.194 align:start size:97% position:3%
"Well, if you request a
refund, we'll send it back.

00:08:49.194 --> 00:08:51.831
If not, then we're gonna
send it to the organization

00:08:51.831 --> 00:08:53.332
of our choice."

00:08:53.332 --> 00:08:54.500
People's donations.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:56.034 align:start size:84% position:16%
- [Dave] Yeah.
Criminal, criminal.

00:08:56.034 --> 00:08:58.637
- And it was DeSantis that
stood up and said, "Mm-mm.

00:08:58.637 --> 00:08:59.572
No, you don't."

00:08:59.572 --> 00:09:00.940
You know, so, I mean, yeah.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:02.174
A credit to him for doing that.

00:09:02.174 --> 00:09:04.076 align:start size:84% position:16%
They ended up having
to refund it all.

00:09:04.076 --> 00:09:06.045 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Right, so can you just
talk about the type of people

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:07.679 align:start size:84% position:16%
that were donating
and the type of people

00:09:07.679 --> 00:09:10.983
that were showing up
and everything else?

00:09:10.983 --> 00:09:13.552
- Just regular, everyday people.

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:15.487
You know, we had...

00:09:15.487 --> 00:09:18.790 align:start position:0%
It was really the most
beautiful, beautiful experience,

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:21.527 align:start size:97% position:3%
like I said, Canadians from
all across the country,

00:09:21.527 --> 00:09:24.997
like the West Coast, the
East Coast, the North.

00:09:24.997 --> 00:09:28.000
We had truckers come down from
Northwest Territories, even.

00:09:30.202 --> 00:09:33.506
But it was, you know, one
of the most telling things

00:09:33.506 --> 00:09:35.308
for me was on the ground there.

00:09:35.308 --> 00:09:38.277 align:start size:84% position:16%
It was really a
jubilant atmosphere.

00:09:38.277 --> 00:09:40.312
People were hugging and
crying, and you know,

00:09:40.312 --> 00:09:42.081
I was talking to
total strangers,

00:09:42.081 --> 00:09:45.217 align:start size:84% position:16%
and it was the
immigrant population,

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:49.355 align:start size:84% position:16%
so immigrants from
Iran, Poland, Romania,

00:09:49.355 --> 00:09:51.490 align:start size:88% position:13%
all these countries
that would come up to me

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:53.626
and they would just have
this look of desperation

00:09:53.626 --> 00:09:54.626
in their eyes.

00:09:54.626 --> 00:09:56.628
Very telling, you know.

00:09:56.628 --> 00:09:57.996
They'd seen this coming.

00:09:57.996 --> 00:09:59.932 align:start size:84% position:16%
They've lived
through it already.

00:09:59.932 --> 00:10:04.903 align:start position:0%
It was kids and senior citizens
and just everyday people.

00:10:04.903 --> 00:10:07.472 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, federal government
employees were there,

00:10:07.472 --> 00:10:12.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
doctors, nurses, lawyers,
ex-law enforcement,

00:10:13.679 --> 00:10:16.214
former firefighters,
you know, everyone.

00:10:16.214 --> 00:10:18.250
- So they come in, they
kick you off GoFund me,

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:19.718
they freeze the bank account.

00:10:19.718 --> 00:10:21.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then they started
freezing the bank accounts

00:10:21.487 --> 00:10:24.856
of the people that donated,
people that in some cases

00:10:24.856 --> 00:10:26.358
donated what, 15 bucks?

00:10:26.358 --> 00:10:27.593
- Yeah.

00:10:27.593 --> 00:10:29.861 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think the average
donation was 50 bucks.

00:10:29.861 --> 00:10:31.263
Yep.

00:10:31.263 --> 00:10:32.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
- And then they're
freezing the bank accounts

00:10:32.465 --> 00:10:36.869 align:start size:88% position:13%
of these people who
then can't get medicine,

00:10:36.869 --> 00:10:38.371 align:start size:84% position:16%
can't go about their
daily business,

00:10:38.371 --> 00:10:41.207
literally cannot withdraw
money from their ATMs.

00:10:42.642 --> 00:10:46.112
- About 280 Canadians had
their accounts frozen.

00:10:46.112 --> 00:10:49.782 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so what that
looked like was mothers

00:10:49.782 --> 00:10:51.817 align:start size:84% position:16%
stuck at the grocery
store checkout

00:10:51.817 --> 00:10:54.253 align:start size:84% position:16%
that had to leave
their groceries there,

00:10:54.253 --> 00:10:57.056
which is a mortifying
experience in itself.

00:10:57.056 --> 00:10:58.591
Like you just said, you know,

00:10:58.591 --> 00:11:00.226 align:start size:97% position:3%
parents that couldn't buy
medicine for their children,

00:11:00.226 --> 00:11:01.360
couldn't pay their mortgage,

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:03.195 align:start size:81% position:19%
couldn't pay their
child support.

00:11:03.195 --> 00:11:07.032
I mean, I was arrested and
my husband was in Ottawa.

00:11:07.032 --> 00:11:08.734
We had a joint account.

00:11:08.734 --> 00:11:10.969
I mean, we don't anymore,
but we had a joint account.

00:11:10.969 --> 00:11:13.139
So here he is in a strange
city, doesn't know anyone,

00:11:13.139 --> 00:11:15.307
and has no access to funds.

00:11:15.307 --> 00:11:16.475
So.

00:11:16.475 --> 00:11:17.743 align:start size:84% position:16%
- What were you
actually arrested for?

00:11:17.743 --> 00:11:19.744
- I was originally
arrested on a charge

00:11:19.744 --> 00:11:22.047
of counseling to
commit mischief.

00:11:22.047 --> 00:11:23.249 align:start size:97% position:3%
- (Dave laughs) there's
something funny about that.

00:11:24.683 --> 00:11:25.618
- And then they had to
add mischief because-

00:11:25.618 --> 00:11:26.885
- Yeah, counseling to, yeah.

00:11:26.885 --> 00:11:28.553
- You can't counsel
to commit an offense

00:11:28.553 --> 00:11:29.488
that never happened.

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:30.723
- Right, right, right, right.

00:11:30.723 --> 00:11:33.558
- So they added a
mischief charge.

00:11:33.558 --> 00:11:37.696 align:start size:97% position:3%
Intimidation, counseling
intimidation, which as I said,

00:11:37.696 --> 00:11:40.098 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm not a very
intimidating person.

00:11:40.098 --> 00:11:41.634
And there's two more.

00:11:41.634 --> 00:11:45.838 align:start position:0%
I think one is disobey a police
order and something else.

00:11:45.838 --> 00:11:47.106
I don't know.

00:11:47.106 --> 00:11:48.974
- And where are you
with all of that now?

00:11:48.974 --> 00:11:50.176
- We have a trial coming up.

00:11:50.176 --> 00:11:51.911
So Chris and I are co-accused,

00:11:51.911 --> 00:11:53.479
and we have a trial
starting in the fall.

00:11:53.479 --> 00:11:55.881
So I'll be going to Ottawa
around the end of August.

00:11:55.881 --> 00:11:58.651
We got a 16-day trial

00:11:58.651 --> 00:12:01.220 align:start size:97% position:3%
over the course of six
weeks for mischief. (laughs)

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:04.056 align:start position:0%
- Right, and because I mentioned
that your lawyer's here,

00:12:04.056 --> 00:12:05.223
and he did say to
you beforehand,

00:12:05.223 --> 00:12:06.558 align:start size:84% position:16%
"I'm not here to
tell you what to say.

00:12:06.558 --> 00:12:07.827
You tell your story."

00:12:09.461 --> 00:12:12.998 align:start size:84% position:16%
What do you want
people to know before,

00:12:12.998 --> 00:12:15.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
I suppose, you go to
trial, so that, you know,

00:12:15.267 --> 00:12:17.536
because a lot of this had
to do with public pressure.

00:12:17.536 --> 00:12:19.038 align:start size:81% position:19%
It seems to me
Trudeau only broke

00:12:19.038 --> 00:12:21.773 align:start size:97% position:3%
because of public pressure,
because suddenly those videos,

00:12:21.773 --> 00:12:24.476
millions and millions
of people were seeing

00:12:24.476 --> 00:12:26.712
that you guys were not
burning down the cities

00:12:26.712 --> 00:12:28.480
like we had seen here in America

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:31.850
and you were not bad guys and
racists and white supremacists

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:33.118
and the rest of it.

00:12:33.118 --> 00:12:34.453
- And they sure tried
to paint it that way.

00:12:34.453 --> 00:12:37.155
So in the fall of last year,

00:12:37.155 --> 00:12:40.158
so anytime the Emergencies
Act is invoked in Canada,

00:12:40.158 --> 00:12:44.597
within 365 days they have
to have an investigation.

00:12:44.597 --> 00:12:46.732 align:start size:84% position:16%
So last fall, we
went to Ottawa again

00:12:46.732 --> 00:12:48.968
for seven weeks to testify.

00:12:48.968 --> 00:12:50.536
I testified there.

00:12:50.536 --> 00:12:54.907
And the evidence that
came out of there,

00:12:54.907 --> 00:12:57.476
the Superintendent for
the Ottawa, or sorry,

00:12:57.476 --> 00:13:01.079
Ontario Provincial Police in
the Intelligence Department

00:13:01.079 --> 00:13:05.617 align:start size:84% position:16%
said the lack of
violence was shocking.

00:13:05.617 --> 00:13:08.520
And he also said that
what he was hearing

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:10.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
coming from the
politicians and the media

00:13:10.422 --> 00:13:12.257 align:start size:84% position:16%
was not lining up
with the intelligence

00:13:12.257 --> 00:13:13.592
that they were getting.

00:13:13.592 --> 00:13:15.094
So it was incredible.

00:13:15.094 --> 00:13:17.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
But our mainstream
doesn't cover that stuff,

00:13:17.329 --> 00:13:19.832
so that's the kind
of information that
we wanna get out,

00:13:19.832 --> 00:13:21.734 align:start size:84% position:16%
is the actual
evidence that came out

00:13:21.734 --> 00:13:23.868
to show that we weren't violent.

00:13:23.868 --> 00:13:27.873 align:start size:97% position:3%
They were issuing internal
memos in the government saying

00:13:27.873 --> 00:13:29.808 align:start size:84% position:16%
that we were entering
federal buildings

00:13:29.808 --> 00:13:31.910
and causing destruction.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:33.979
Like, the lies.

00:13:33.979 --> 00:13:37.549
The lies, the bold-faced
lies was quite shocking.

00:13:37.549 --> 00:13:39.017
- Yeah.

00:13:39.017 --> 00:13:40.085 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, can you talk about
the media component of this,

00:13:40.085 --> 00:13:41.353
because, you know,

00:13:41.353 --> 00:13:42.788
for as horrible as our
mainstream media here,

00:13:42.788 --> 00:13:44.657
corporate press is
in the United States.

00:13:44.657 --> 00:13:46.358
I mean, you guys have the CBC.

00:13:46.358 --> 00:13:50.562
It's fully state-funded,
I would argue propaganda.

00:13:50.562 --> 00:13:53.031
I'm guessing you probably
don't disagree with me.

00:13:53.031 --> 00:13:56.135
But then I was seeing guys on
the ground like Ezra Levant

00:13:56.135 --> 00:13:58.571
over at Rebel News, who
they were deeply embedded

00:13:58.571 --> 00:13:59.839 align:start size:88% position:13%
with you guys and
plenty of other people.

00:13:59.839 --> 00:14:00.706
They're independent.

00:14:00.706 --> 00:14:02.374
They're under attack now too.

00:14:02.374 --> 00:14:03.842
- Mm-hm.

00:14:03.842 --> 00:14:06.211
Well, and thank God for our
independent journalists,

00:14:06.211 --> 00:14:08.013
and the citizen journalists too.

00:14:08.013 --> 00:14:09.548
Like, yeah, Rebel
News was there.

00:14:09.548 --> 00:14:10.382
They were amazing.

00:14:10.382 --> 00:14:11.383
True North was there.

00:14:11.383 --> 00:14:13.218
They were amazing.

00:14:13.218 --> 00:14:16.154
There were so many
of them, and I mean,

00:14:16.154 --> 00:14:17.389
the CBC is literally

00:14:17.389 --> 00:14:19.725
I think two blocks from
where the protest was.

00:14:20.926 --> 00:14:22.594
And so they could see, right?

00:14:22.594 --> 00:14:25.263
But they weren't coming down
and telling the whole story.

00:14:25.263 --> 00:14:27.399
And for the life of me-

00:14:27.399 --> 00:14:31.703
- Was there anyone on CBC
or any mainstream channel

00:14:31.703 --> 00:14:34.340 align:start position:0%
that was giving you a fair shake
to go on these shows and...

00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:35.174 align:start size:69% position:31%
- No.
- Nobody.

00:14:35.174 --> 00:14:36.242
- Nope. Nope.

00:14:38.076 --> 00:14:39.110
No, none of them.

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:40.679
They had painted
their narrative.

00:14:40.679 --> 00:14:42.214 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's more evidence
that came out.

00:14:42.214 --> 00:14:43.749
They had painted that narrative

00:14:43.749 --> 00:14:45.851
before I even met Chris Barber

00:14:45.851 --> 00:14:48.086
brought in Big Red and we left.

00:14:48.086 --> 00:14:49.354
So they were colluding.

00:14:49.354 --> 00:14:50.289
The government was
already colluding

00:14:50.289 --> 00:14:51.590
with our mainstream media.

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:52.824
And you're right that, I mean,

00:14:52.824 --> 00:14:55.260
the CBC is the one that
came out and suggested

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:58.463 align:start size:97% position:3%
that we were being
influenced by the Russians.

00:14:58.463 --> 00:15:00.265
And I remember I looked at
Chris Barber heard story.

00:15:00.265 --> 00:15:01.767
- It's almost like we've
heard this story before.

00:15:01.767 --> 00:15:02.434
- I was like, I don't even
know if I know any Russians.

00:15:02.434 --> 00:15:03.936
You know, like.

00:15:03.936 --> 00:15:05.570
- You probably hugged some
out on the street out there.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:07.172
- Yes, we sure did.

00:15:07.172 --> 00:15:10.275
- What was it ultimately
that broke Trudeau on this

00:15:10.275 --> 00:15:11.777 align:start size:84% position:16%
when he finally
turned around one day?

00:15:11.777 --> 00:15:14.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause it really seemed
like he wasn't gonna stop.

00:15:14.013 --> 00:15:16.248
And then eventually it did,

00:15:16.248 --> 00:15:18.484 align:start size:84% position:16%
the pressure got
released a little bit.

00:15:18.484 --> 00:15:19.852
- Well, I think what happened,,,

00:15:19.852 --> 00:15:22.888 align:start size:88% position:13%
Are you referring to
when he revoked the act?

00:15:22.888 --> 00:15:25.757 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, when, well, basically
at some point there was,

00:15:25.757 --> 00:15:27.225
I don't know, was that
when he revoked the act,

00:15:27.225 --> 00:15:28.760
or at some point,

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:30.528
basically the truckers were
there, they sort of, it was,

00:15:30.528 --> 00:15:32.932
you guys were all sort of at
an impasse and didn't he...

00:15:32.932 --> 00:15:34.299
Was that when he
revoked the act or-

00:15:34.299 --> 00:15:35.534
- No.

00:15:35.534 --> 00:15:37.035
Well, what he did
instead was invoked

00:15:37.035 --> 00:15:40.205
what is akin to martial law in
Canada, the Emergencies Act.

00:15:40.205 --> 00:15:41.206
- Right, so that
was the emergency.

00:15:41.206 --> 00:15:42.408
- [Tamara] That's right.

00:15:42.408 --> 00:15:44.008 align:start size:84% position:16%
- But what then
broke it after that?

00:15:44.008 --> 00:15:46.812
- Well, I think a lot of
it had to do with the banks

00:15:46.812 --> 00:15:49.748
because people were seeing
that these bank accounts

00:15:49.748 --> 00:15:51.050
were getting frozen
and they were going

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:52.784
and pulling their money out.

00:15:52.784 --> 00:15:55.286 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, tens of thousands,
like millions of dollars.

00:15:55.286 --> 00:15:57.822 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think that he got
some pressure from the banks

00:15:57.822 --> 00:15:59.858
to revoke this thing.

00:15:59.858 --> 00:16:02.594
- Has there been any reckoning
with Trudeau within the party

00:16:02.594 --> 00:16:05.564
or within Canadian
politics altogether?

00:16:05.564 --> 00:16:07.099
I mean, I know you guys have

00:16:07.099 --> 00:16:09.935 align:start position:0%
a sort of somewhat
dysfunctional conservative party

00:16:09.935 --> 00:16:11.436
and, you know,

00:16:11.436 --> 00:16:13.672
things never really seem to
materialize on that side,

00:16:13.672 --> 00:16:15.440 align:start size:97% position:3%
but there's been no
reckoning with any of this?

00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:18.610 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Not yet, no, but I am
hopeful that that will come.

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:22.313 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, I know that the
inquiry is over, but you know,

00:16:22.313 --> 00:16:24.416
there's still some legal
things happening there.

00:16:24.416 --> 00:16:27.519
They just did a judicial
review of the invocation

00:16:27.519 --> 00:16:28.721
of the Emergencies Act

00:16:28.721 --> 00:16:30.689
so we're awaiting for
that decision now.

00:16:30.689 --> 00:16:33.825
So I'm really hoping that
he can be held accountable

00:16:33.825 --> 00:16:38.330
for his decision to
have law enforcement

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:39.965
beat up our veterans,

00:16:40.932 --> 00:16:43.801 align:start size:88% position:13%
our veterans,
grandmothers, you know,

00:16:43.801 --> 00:16:46.471 align:start size:97% position:3%
and it was such a peaceful,
beautiful protest.

00:16:46.471 --> 00:16:48.907
And the footage that
came out afterwards.

00:16:48.907 --> 00:16:50.075
I was in jail, obviously.

00:16:50.075 --> 00:16:52.711 align:start size:84% position:16%
I didn't see it
firsthand, but I mean,

00:16:52.711 --> 00:16:55.414
I got home and I sat it on
my couch and I just cried

00:16:55.414 --> 00:16:58.383 align:start size:84% position:16%
like a baby watching
all that footage,

00:16:58.383 --> 00:16:59.917 align:start size:84% position:16%
you know, these people
getting arrested

00:16:59.917 --> 00:17:03.255 align:start size:97% position:3%
and left in transport vehicles
for hours with their hands

00:17:03.255 --> 00:17:04.856
zip-tied behind their back,

00:17:04.856 --> 00:17:07.092 align:start size:84% position:16%
driven to the
outskirts of Ottawa

00:17:07.092 --> 00:17:08.927
and dropped off in a snowbank.

00:17:10.228 --> 00:17:12.431 align:start position:0%
You know, it was heartbreaking,
absolutely heartbreaking.

00:17:12.431 --> 00:17:14.199
- How long were you in jail for?

00:17:14.199 --> 00:17:15.734
- In the winter

00:17:15.734 --> 00:17:17.569
I was in jail for 18 days
and then I was rearrested

00:17:17.569 --> 00:17:20.906 align:start size:84% position:16%
last summer on an
alleged breach charge.

00:17:20.906 --> 00:17:24.976 align:start size:88% position:13%
So I did 30 days in
prison last summer too.

00:17:24.976 --> 00:17:28.013
- What has this taught you
about your fellow citizens?

00:17:28.013 --> 00:17:30.949
Kinda good, good
and bad, I suppose.

00:17:30.949 --> 00:17:33.218
- Well, I used to sit on
the board of directors

00:17:33.218 --> 00:17:35.854
for a Western Federal
Independence Party.

00:17:35.854 --> 00:17:40.192 align:start position:0%
We created this political
party out of nothing basically.

00:17:40.192 --> 00:17:44.662
And so for me, the biggest
eyeopener was, you know,

00:17:44.662 --> 00:17:47.900
we've always had kind of a
east-west divide in Canada

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:49.734
and, you know, we're always told

00:17:49.734 --> 00:17:51.403 align:start size:84% position:16%
that we're just a
bunch of hillbillies

00:17:51.403 --> 00:17:53.872 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they don't want our
dirty oil and all that stuff.

00:17:53.872 --> 00:17:56.741
So my biggest eye-opening
experience to begin with

00:17:56.741 --> 00:17:58.110
was I'm sitting at
my kitchen table.

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:00.445
We'd all been sent home
'cause it was Omicron.

00:18:00.445 --> 00:18:01.580
Sitting at my kitchen table

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:04.116 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I got my two
monitors on on my table.

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:07.419 align:start size:97% position:3%
We had road captains from
every province that would lead

00:18:07.419 --> 00:18:09.387
like a contingent of trucks in.

00:18:09.387 --> 00:18:11.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I've got these
chats open and I'm talking

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:13.425
to the road captain from Quebec,

00:18:13.425 --> 00:18:15.961 align:start size:84% position:16%
and she has like 1,000
trucks ready to go.

00:18:15.961 --> 00:18:18.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
And these guys are
beautiful and supportive.

00:18:18.196 --> 00:18:21.100
And I thought, this
has all been a lie.

00:18:22.234 --> 00:18:24.402
Like, this has all
been to divide us.

00:18:24.402 --> 00:18:26.472
And it was so not true.

00:18:26.472 --> 00:18:29.841
And then shortly
after we got there,

00:18:29.841 --> 00:18:32.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the first pictures
I saw was a Quebecois

00:18:32.644 --> 00:18:36.214
holding their flag and an
Albertan holding our flag

00:18:36.214 --> 00:18:37.416
and them shaking hands,

00:18:37.416 --> 00:18:39.484 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I mean, that
was such an amazing,

00:18:39.484 --> 00:18:40.919
astonishing thing to see.

00:18:40.919 --> 00:18:42.187
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:18:42.187 --> 00:18:44.222
- You know, like the
unity that happened.

00:18:44.222 --> 00:18:46.091
It didn't matter what
color your skin was.

00:18:46.091 --> 00:18:47.826
It didn't matter what
God you worshiped.

00:18:47.826 --> 00:18:49.127
It didn't matter who you loved.

00:18:49.127 --> 00:18:51.697 align:start size:88% position:13%
It didn't matter what
your income bracket was.

00:18:51.697 --> 00:18:53.998
We were all just Canadians.

00:18:53.998 --> 00:18:57.202
And for the last eight years
that man has been doing nothing

00:18:57.202 --> 00:19:00.271
but to try and divide us
along all of those lines.

00:19:00.271 --> 00:19:01.839
- Do you think he's...

00:19:01.839 --> 00:19:03.608
You know, he only got,
what, 30% of the vote,

00:19:03.608 --> 00:19:04.443
something like that?

00:19:04.443 --> 00:19:05.877
- Like 31. Yeah.

00:19:05.877 --> 00:19:07.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Do you think he's
actually convincing people

00:19:07.612 --> 00:19:11.016 align:start size:97% position:3%
that he's right, or is it
just that Canadians generally

00:19:11.016 --> 00:19:13.284
are just nice so
they don't step up,

00:19:13.284 --> 00:19:15.420 align:start size:88% position:13%
that these moments
don't happen that often?

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.088
- (laughs) I don't know.

00:19:17.088 --> 00:19:19.324
People ask me like, why
do you keep electing him?

00:19:19.324 --> 00:19:20.825
And I said like, are we though?

00:19:20.825 --> 00:19:22.194 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like, I don't know if
you know what's going on

00:19:22.194 --> 00:19:24.696
up there right now,
but we're in deep

00:19:24.696 --> 00:19:28.099
in some serious Chinese
interference allegations.

00:19:28.099 --> 00:19:30.001
They've been interfering
in our elections and stuff.

00:19:30.001 --> 00:19:31.670
So I mean, is he
getting elected?

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:33.171
I don't know.

00:19:33.171 --> 00:19:35.039
I guess they're dragging their
feet on that too, of course.

00:19:35.039 --> 00:19:37.075
He tried to once again
get one of his buddies

00:19:37.075 --> 00:19:38.610
to investigate himself,

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:40.745
and that actually didn't
work out too good for him,

00:19:40.745 --> 00:19:43.115 align:start size:84% position:16%
but now they've
broke for the summer.

00:19:43.115 --> 00:19:46.384
So, it's just astonishing.

00:19:46.384 --> 00:19:47.786 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So when they
reversed this thing

00:19:47.786 --> 00:19:49.754 align:start position:0%
and they reversed the Emergency
Powers Act and all that,

00:19:49.754 --> 00:19:51.189 align:start size:84% position:16%
then the bank
accounts were opened

00:19:51.189 --> 00:19:53.057
and then did they start
leaving people alone?

00:19:53.057 --> 00:19:54.526
I mean, did they
drop, obviously,

00:19:54.526 --> 00:19:56.094 align:start size:84% position:16%
you're going through
the case still.

00:19:56.094 --> 00:19:58.263
Did they drop cases
against people or?

00:19:58.263 --> 00:19:59.331
- I don't know if
they've dropped

00:19:59.331 --> 00:20:01.667
any charges against people.

00:20:01.667 --> 00:20:02.934
Maybe one case.

00:20:02.934 --> 00:20:06.871 align:start size:84% position:16%
But they're pursuing
them pretty well,

00:20:06.871 --> 00:20:09.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially in me and
Chris's case, very, very,

00:20:09.808 --> 00:20:10.742
like they're hard.

00:20:10.742 --> 00:20:11.843
They're coming after us hard.

00:20:11.843 --> 00:20:13.111
- Yeah.

00:20:13.111 --> 00:20:14.946
What I always ask guests
that somehow, you know,

00:20:14.946 --> 00:20:17.249
a certain set of people just
kind of step into these things.

00:20:17.249 --> 00:20:18.950
They don't intend
on doing these.

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:20.985 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, some people
set out to do something.

00:20:20.985 --> 00:20:22.820
Some people kind
of step into it.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:25.089
You strike me as like the
step into it type person.

00:20:25.089 --> 00:20:28.660
What do you think it is about
you that kind of makes you

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:31.663
want to do this or
have to do this or?

00:20:31.663 --> 00:20:33.932
- Well, I love my country.

00:20:33.932 --> 00:20:37.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I grew up
fascinated with Americans

00:20:37.169 --> 00:20:41.206
and their passion for their
flag and their patriotism.

00:20:41.206 --> 00:20:43.609 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, for me that
was so admirable.

00:20:43.609 --> 00:20:48.146
So that was something that I
experienced for the first time

00:20:48.146 --> 00:20:51.850
driving across Canada and
meeting all those people.

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:54.219
You know, so it's worth saving.

00:20:54.219 --> 00:20:55.954 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, we were just
talking before we started here

00:20:55.954 --> 00:20:57.689 align:start size:88% position:13%
about all the people
that are leaving Canada,

00:20:57.689 --> 00:21:00.625
fleeing Canada, which is
two words I never thought

00:21:00.625 --> 00:21:02.260
I'd hear in the same sentence.

00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:03.761 align:start size:84% position:16%
But if we all
leave, then who's...

00:21:03.761 --> 00:21:07.632
It's worth fighting for,
and the people are so good.

00:21:07.632 --> 00:21:11.169
You know, it was for me

00:21:11.169 --> 00:21:16.241
a very divine and spiritual
experience, and the unity

00:21:17.342 --> 00:21:19.377
that I saw just made
me love it even more.

00:21:19.377 --> 00:21:21.846 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Are you seeing a lot of
people flee Canada right now?

00:21:21.846 --> 00:21:23.081
I mentioned to you right
before we started, I mean,

00:21:23.081 --> 00:21:24.315
I'm seeing a ton of Canadians.

00:21:24.315 --> 00:21:25.950
- Yes.

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:27.452
- You know, Canadians
are snowbirds down
in Florida usually,

00:21:27.452 --> 00:21:29.421
but I'm meeting more and
more people that are like,

00:21:29.421 --> 00:21:31.256
"Oh, I'm actually
not going back.

00:21:31.256 --> 00:21:32.757
Well, this is it now."

00:21:32.757 --> 00:21:34.792
- There's a lot of 'em,
a lot of good people too,

00:21:34.792 --> 00:21:37.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
like our doctors, our
nurses, you know, police,

00:21:37.762 --> 00:21:41.833
like our professionals,
so it's quite alarming.

00:21:41.833 --> 00:21:43.335 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Did this change
any of your politics

00:21:43.335 --> 00:21:46.071 align:start size:84% position:16%
in terms of
capitalism, socialism?

00:21:46.071 --> 00:21:48.507
You guys have more socialized
medicine, that sort of thing?

00:21:48.507 --> 00:21:50.342
It seemed like some
new lines were drawn

00:21:50.342 --> 00:21:52.477 align:start size:84% position:16%
in regards to those
things as well.

00:21:52.477 --> 00:21:55.814 align:start size:97% position:3%
- No, I think I've always
been very conservative-minded

00:21:55.814 --> 00:22:00.318
and I certainly have
never voted liberal

00:22:00.318 --> 00:22:01.953
in 30 years probably.

00:22:04.322 --> 00:22:07.859
Well, because they had a
big scandal in the 2000s.

00:22:07.859 --> 00:22:10.127
You probably heard about
the sponsorship scandal.

00:22:10.127 --> 00:22:13.398 align:start position:0%
And that was kind of when I
really started paying attention

00:22:13.398 --> 00:22:16.234
to politics and following it
a little bit more closely,

00:22:16.234 --> 00:22:18.937
and I was just disgusted.

00:22:18.937 --> 00:22:20.805 align:start size:84% position:16%
There's never been
any arrests over that.

00:22:20.805 --> 00:22:24.676 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like billions of Canadians'
taxpayers' dollars,

00:22:24.676 --> 00:22:25.811
you know, and nothing.

00:22:25.811 --> 00:22:27.845
So yeah, no,

00:22:27.845 --> 00:22:29.914
I think I'll continue to be a
conservative minded. (laughs)

00:22:29.914 --> 00:22:32.317
- The machine has a way
of just going on and on.

00:22:32.317 --> 00:22:33.952 align:start size:88% position:13%
That's why I was
asking about, you know,

00:22:33.952 --> 00:22:36.487
is there any reckoning
for Trudeau or anything?

00:22:36.487 --> 00:22:37.655
'Cause we have that
here in the States.

00:22:37.655 --> 00:22:38.957 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's like no matter
how many times

00:22:38.957 --> 00:22:40.191
they lied about the mandates,

00:22:40.191 --> 00:22:42.727 align:start size:84% position:16%
lied about the
efficacy of the vax

00:22:42.727 --> 00:22:45.830 align:start size:97% position:3%
or how unconstitutional
lockdowns were anything else,

00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:47.131
nobody gets fired.

00:22:47.131 --> 00:22:48.500 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Nope.
- Nobody gets fired.

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:49.668
- No accountability.

00:22:49.668 --> 00:22:50.502 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It's a weird
realization, you know?

00:22:50.502 --> 00:22:52.604
- It is, it really is.

00:22:52.604 --> 00:22:55.140
- Are you hopeful that things
can turn around in Canada or-

00:22:55.140 --> 00:22:56.408
- I am.

00:22:56.408 --> 00:22:58.176
- Yeah, so where does
the hope come from?

00:22:58.176 --> 00:23:01.412 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Well again, I mean, my
belief in the Canadian people.

00:23:01.412 --> 00:23:05.317
Like they all came together
in such an amazing way and,

00:23:05.317 --> 00:23:08.220
you know, we can make a change.

00:23:08.220 --> 00:23:10.288
We just proved that, you know?

00:23:10.288 --> 00:23:13.024
Like I said, this was just
such an organic movement.

00:23:13.024 --> 00:23:16.194
It literally started off
with a handful of people,

00:23:16.194 --> 00:23:21.266
and I mean, within 24 hours we
realized, holy cow, you know,

00:23:22.333 --> 00:23:23.635 align:start size:88% position:13%
when we were talking
about setting the target

00:23:23.635 --> 00:23:25.569
for the GoFundMe,
Chris had said,

00:23:25.569 --> 00:23:29.640 align:start position:0%
well, I think it was 200 or
$250,000, and I'm like, "No way.

00:23:29.640 --> 00:23:30.875
Don't be ridiculous."

00:23:30.875 --> 00:23:34.312
I said, "I'll set
it for 100,000,

00:23:34.312 --> 00:23:36.181 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I don't even
think we'll hit that."

00:23:36.181 --> 00:23:38.849 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like in the back of my mind,
I thought maybe 20 grand.

00:23:38.849 --> 00:23:42.887
They would drive across Canada,
stand there with their sign,

00:23:42.887 --> 00:23:44.489 align:start size:88% position:13%
get back in their
trucks, and drive home.

00:23:44.489 --> 00:23:46.625
And within 24 hours, you know,

00:23:46.625 --> 00:23:49.260
we blew past 100,000 dollars.

00:23:49.260 --> 00:23:53.531 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so, you know, the support,
the support was incredible.

00:23:53.531 --> 00:23:54.900
And like I said,

00:23:54.900 --> 00:23:57.369
it was so organic and it
just came from nothing.

00:23:57.369 --> 00:23:59.337
And then all of a sudden, boom.

00:23:59.337 --> 00:24:01.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
And while the politicians
will not acknowledge

00:24:01.706 --> 00:24:05.177
that what the truckers did
changed things, you know,

00:24:05.177 --> 00:24:06.644
before we even left provinces,

00:24:06.644 --> 00:24:10.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
were talking about lifting
their mandates, so.

00:24:10.081 --> 00:24:12.650
- So it was working when
you get people out there

00:24:12.650 --> 00:24:13.585
doing the right thing.

00:24:13.585 --> 00:24:14.852
You know, it's interesting.

00:24:14.852 --> 00:24:16.120
I was just thinking as
you were saying this,

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:18.523
we played a video about
two weeks ago on my show

00:24:18.523 --> 00:24:20.558
where outside of the
prime minister's office

00:24:20.558 --> 00:24:23.127 align:start size:97% position:3%
they took down the Canadian
flags and they put up

00:24:23.127 --> 00:24:25.730
the trans flag or
whatever that is.

00:24:25.730 --> 00:24:27.799
It's like these things
really are connected

00:24:27.799 --> 00:24:30.335
in a very bizarre way.

00:24:30.335 --> 00:24:31.569
Do you see that?

00:24:31.569 --> 00:24:33.839
- Yeah, oh, I think
that's all connected.

00:24:33.839 --> 00:24:37.142
Everything, the climate
emergency, you know,

00:24:37.142 --> 00:24:38.977 align:start size:84% position:16%
that we're supposedly
under, all of it.

00:24:38.977 --> 00:24:40.745
I think it's all connected.

00:24:40.745 --> 00:24:42.247
- Yeah, how much are you guys...

00:24:42.247 --> 00:24:44.349
So you mentioned a little
bit about the energy makers

00:24:44.349 --> 00:24:47.085
in the West and the sort
of energy takers in East.

00:24:47.085 --> 00:24:49.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
How much of that affected
all of this as well,

00:24:49.454 --> 00:24:51.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
just the way the country's
split in that sense?

00:24:51.890 --> 00:24:53.692
- Well, I mean, a
lot of the stuff

00:24:53.692 --> 00:24:56.026
with the oil and gas industry,

00:24:56.026 --> 00:24:58.629 align:start size:97% position:3%
if I'm understanding your
question correctly, you know,

00:24:58.629 --> 00:25:01.666
they wanted to build a
pipeline across Canada

00:25:01.666 --> 00:25:04.736 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the Quebecois
said no way, you know.

00:25:04.736 --> 00:25:07.038 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so that we could get
our product out there

00:25:07.038 --> 00:25:08.172
and keep it in Canada.

00:25:08.172 --> 00:25:09.407
You know what I mean?

00:25:09.407 --> 00:25:12.343
Instead, they import
oil from Saudi Arabia

00:25:12.343 --> 00:25:14.145
and these other countries,
you know, that some of them

00:25:14.145 --> 00:25:17.415 align:start size:97% position:3%
have some very horrible human
rights abuses, you know,

00:25:17.415 --> 00:25:19.116
and that just boggles my mind.

00:25:19.116 --> 00:25:21.853
You know, I worked
in that industry.

00:25:21.853 --> 00:25:23.387
I know it's not dirty.

00:25:23.387 --> 00:25:25.757
I mean, Canada has one of the
most environmentally friendly

00:25:25.757 --> 00:25:30.028 align:start size:88% position:13%
and efficient energy
industries in the world.

00:25:30.028 --> 00:25:32.663
We should be a beacon of
hope for other countries,

00:25:32.663 --> 00:25:34.765
and our politicians
should be, you know,

00:25:34.765 --> 00:25:37.635 align:start position:0%
shouting that from the
rooftops and advocating for it.

00:25:37.635 --> 00:25:40.505
And instead they're just
trying to shut us down.

00:25:40.505 --> 00:25:42.740 align:start size:84% position:16%
And in the province
that I live in,

00:25:42.740 --> 00:25:46.478 align:start size:81% position:19%
it's our resources
is oil and gas.

00:25:46.478 --> 00:25:48.146
Like, that's our main resource.

00:25:48.146 --> 00:25:50.949 align:start size:84% position:16%
So that affects a
lot of human beings.

00:25:50.949 --> 00:25:52.750
They're not just numbers.

00:25:52.750 --> 00:25:54.352
These are people that
are losing their homes

00:25:54.352 --> 00:25:55.887
and losing their jobs.

00:25:55.887 --> 00:25:57.388
- And a lot of them without
these jobs, it's, you know,

00:25:57.388 --> 00:26:01.292
some of the life out there,
it's the tundra basically.

00:26:01.292 --> 00:26:04.295 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, it's not as if there's
a million other reasons

00:26:04.295 --> 00:26:05.230
to be out there.

00:26:05.230 --> 00:26:05.964
It's for the energy, right?

00:26:05.964 --> 00:26:06.898
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:26:06.898 --> 00:26:08.265
Well, it's a beautiful province.

00:26:08.265 --> 00:26:10.735 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's a absolutely gorgeous,
gorgeous province.

00:26:10.735 --> 00:26:12.237
Yeah.

00:26:12.237 --> 00:26:14.672
- What else should people
know about what you guys

00:26:14.672 --> 00:26:16.641 align:start size:84% position:16%
were doing and where
the fight's going

00:26:16.641 --> 00:26:17.908
and how they came out?

00:26:17.908 --> 00:26:21.111
- Well, I think the most
important thing for me,

00:26:21.111 --> 00:26:24.081
and one of the reasons why I
felt this book was so important

00:26:24.081 --> 00:26:28.386
was that the freezing of
the bank accounts was huge.

00:26:28.386 --> 00:26:30.588
And you know, Canada
is the most polite

00:26:30.588 --> 00:26:34.158 align:start position:0%
and passive country on the
planet as far as I'm concerned.

00:26:34.158 --> 00:26:35.994
So, you know, if they
can do that in Canada,

00:26:35.994 --> 00:26:38.329 align:start size:88% position:13%
they can do it anywhere,
anywhere at all.

00:26:38.329 --> 00:26:40.064 align:start size:88% position:13%
There was no
parliamentary oversight.

00:26:40.064 --> 00:26:41.799
There was no court
order from a judge.

00:26:41.799 --> 00:26:43.434
It was just boom.

00:26:43.434 --> 00:26:46.171
And nobody from the
banks even resisted.

00:26:47.272 --> 00:26:48.907
Like, there's notes in
our Finance Minister

00:26:48.907 --> 00:26:51.642
Chrystia Freeland's dossier
that came out as evidence

00:26:51.642 --> 00:26:56.213
saying, "Label them
as terrorists and
seize their assets."

00:26:56.213 --> 00:27:01.219 align:start position:0%
Like it's mind-boggling the
lengths that they went to to try

00:27:02.587 --> 00:27:05.523 align:start size:97% position:3%
and paint us as, well, January
6th style insurrectionists.

00:27:05.523 --> 00:27:07.759
That's what they
wanted, you know?

00:27:07.759 --> 00:27:09.493 align:start size:81% position:19%
So I think it's
an important read.

00:27:09.493 --> 00:27:10.996
It's an important story.

00:27:12.330 --> 00:27:16.101 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's a beautiful story of
humanity and I'm just so proud

00:27:16.101 --> 00:27:17.335
of how it all turned out.

00:27:17.335 --> 00:27:18.569
- Yeah.

00:27:18.569 --> 00:27:19.837 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, and you're still
in the midst of it,

00:27:19.837 --> 00:27:21.606
so I suppose we'll see
how it all turns out.

00:27:21.606 --> 00:27:22.840
- [Tamara] Yes, that's right.

00:27:22.840 --> 00:27:25.910 align:start size:88% position:13%
- But I assume you're
hopeful that the charges

00:27:25.910 --> 00:27:28.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
will just be dismissed and
that'll be it and then-

00:27:28.279 --> 00:27:29.781
- That would be nice,

00:27:29.781 --> 00:27:33.984
but they've been very eager,
and like I said, last summer,

00:27:33.984 --> 00:27:36.388
I was picked up on an
alleged breach charge

00:27:37.422 --> 00:27:39.057
and spent 30 days in jail

00:27:39.057 --> 00:27:41.358
after I was denied bail
initially then also.

00:27:41.358 --> 00:27:44.195
So they don't seem
to be letting up.

00:27:44.195 --> 00:27:48.066
And I think they wanna make
an example of us to tell...

00:27:48.066 --> 00:27:52.137
It's intimidation, but they
picked the wrong grandma.

00:27:52.137 --> 00:27:53.905
So. (laughs)

00:27:53.905 --> 00:27:56.273 align:start position:0%
- And by the way, they weren't,
until recently, I mean,

00:27:56.273 --> 00:27:59.410
unvaxxed Canadians couldn't
even get out of the country.

00:27:59.410 --> 00:28:00.345
- No. Nope.

00:28:00.345 --> 00:28:01.346
- They did reverse that, right?

